# Help me build a vet-clinic round in Jac. Pets are nodes with a name, species, and whether they need a vaccine today. A vet walker should keep its own list of patient names and count of shots given as it moves from pet to pet; afterwards I want to read those numbers straight off the spawned walker instance and print a summary.
"""Vet clinic round: model patients as pets and walk the ward with a vet."""

node Pet {
    has name: str = "";
    has species: str = "";
    has needs_vaccine: bool = False;
}

walker Vet {
    has patient_names: list[str] = [];
    has shots_given: int = 0;

    can start with Root entry {
        print("Starting clinic round");
        visit [-->];
    }

    can examine with Pet entry {
        self.patient_names.append(here.name);
        if here.needs_vaccine {
            self.shots_given += 1;
            print(f"Vaccinated {here.name} ({here.species})");
        } else {
            print(f"Checked {here.name} ({here.species}) — no shot needed");
        }
        visit [-->] else { disengage; }
    }
}

with entry {
    root ++> Pet(name="Buddy", species="Dog", needs_vaccine=True)
        ++> Pet(name="Whiskers", species="Cat", needs_vaccine=False)
        ++> Pet(name="Peanut", species="Rabbit", needs_vaccine=True);

    vet = Vet();
    root spawn vet;

    print(f"Round complete: {len(vet.patient_names)} patients seen, "
          f"{vet.shots_given} shots given");
    print(f"Patients: {', '.join(vet.patient_names)}");
}

# Language: jac
# from: osp_A_12__composer_v30
# I'm doing a warehouse stock take in Jac. Stock items are nodes with a SKU and a quantity. A counter walker should report each shelf quantity during its sweep, and the main block should read result.reports afterwards to print the per-item counts, the total units in the warehouse, and the smallest shelf count.
"""Warehouse stock take: model stock items as nodes and sweep shelves with a counter walker."""

node StockItem {
    has sku: str = "";
    has quantity: int = 0;
}

walker Counter {
    has reports: list[tuple[str, int]] = [];

    can start with Root entry {
        print("Warehouse stock take — sweeping shelves");
        visit [-->];
    }

    can count with StockItem entry {
        print(f"[SHELF] {here.sku}: {here.quantity} units");
        report (here.sku, here.quantity);
        visit [-->] else { disengage; };
    }
}

with entry {
    root ++> StockItem(sku="WH-100", quantity=24)
        ++> StockItem(sku="WH-200", quantity=7)
        ++> StockItem(sku="WH-300", quantity=15)
        ++> StockItem(sku="WH-400", quantity=3);

    result = root spawn Counter();

    total_units = 0;
    min_count = -1;
    print("Per-item counts:");
    for (sku, qty) in result.reports {
        print(f"  {sku}: {qty}");
        total_units += qty;
        if min_count < 0 {
            min_count = qty;
        } else {
            if qty < min_count {
                min_count = qty;
            }
        }
    }
    print(f"Total units in warehouse: {total_units}");
    print(f"Smallest shelf count: {min_count}");
}

# written in jac
# from: iss_jondo2010__boomerang__128
# A maintainer on the project jondo2010/boomerang (Rust) filed this issue about hand-rolled graph machinery causing pain:
# 
# Issue #128: [Deployment plan 5A] Project backend-neutral coordination data and an immutable `RtiImage`
# 
# ## Outcome
# 
# Deliver **Task 5A: Project backend-neutral coordination data and an immutable `RtiImage`** as one independently reviewable pull request.
# 
# ## Roadmap position
# 
# - Phase 5: Compiled federation baseline and legacy federation cut.
# - Depends on #127.
# - Architecture authorities: [deployment architecture](../blob/main/docs/deployment-architecture.md) and `docs/federated-deployment-roadmap.md`.
# - This milestone is an architectural checkpoint, not a shippable-release claim.
# 
# ## Scope
# 
# - Make the canonical analyzed federation, not `RtiImage`, authoritative for logical-time and lifecycle semantics.
# - Add stable flow identity and physical input/output boundary metadata.
# - Add explicit recovery, boundary-failure, transport, codec, timing, and security policy schema; unsupported behavior must fail closed.
# - Project the central backend mechanically into immutable dense `RtiImage` tables without rerunning graph analysis.
# - Preserve the federated-reactors research brief as non-normative provenance and translate required protocol concepts into conformance vocabulary.
# 
# ## Acceptance evidence
# 
# - [ ] Projection preserves Federate identities, parallel routes, delays, and policy references deterministically.
# - [ ] Unknown or unsupported policy selections fail during compilation.
# - [ ] `RtiImage` construction contains no reachability, SCC, or shortest-path analysis.
# - [ ] Stable flow and physical-boundary identities survive canonical lowering.
# 
# ## Delivery constraints
# 
# - Use focused TDD at the named stable boundary and record observed RED/GREEN evidence in the PR.
# - Keep one authoritative lowest-layer test per invariant plus only materially distinct boundary coverage.
# - Keep the PR below 2,000 added-plus-deleted text lines unless an explicit split or override is approved.
# - Document introduced public types and fields.
# - Keep workflow documents, agent files, logs, recordings, coverage, and generated Graft artifacts out of the commit.
# 
# Write a small self-contained Jac demo program that models the essential scenario from this issue natively: pick the 2-4 core entity types as node archetypes with typed has fields, connect instances with edges (typed edges where the relationship carries meaning), and implement walker(s) that perform the traversal the issue complains about (e.g. recursion over parents/children, cascade delete or invalidation, dependency ordering, cycle detection, reachability). Wire a small demonstration graph in a `with entry` block and spawn the walker(s). No I/O, no external libraries, no pytest blocks.
"""Backend-neutral federation projection into an immutable dense RTI image."""

node Federate {
    has title: str = "";
    has year: int = 0;
    has available: bool = True;
    has federate_id: str = "";
    has logical_time: int = 0;
    has lifecycle_policy: str = "";
}

node Flow {
    has title: str = "";
    has year: int = 0;
    has available: bool = True;
    has flow_id: str = "";
    has delay_ms: int = 0;
    has recovery_policy: str = "";
    has boundary_policy: str = "";
    has transport_policy: str = "";
    has codec_policy: str = "";
    has timing_policy: str = "";
    has security_policy: str = "";
}

node Boundary {
    has title: str = "";
    has year: int = 0;
    has available: bool = True;
    has boundary_id: str = "";
    has physical_role: str = "";
    has direction: str = "";
}

node RtiImage {
    has title: str = "";
    has year: int = 0;
    has available: bool = True;
    has image_id: str = "";
    has frozen: bool = False;
    has federate_table: list[str] = [];
    has flow_table: list[str] = [];
    has boundary_table: list[str] = [];
    has policy_table: list[str] = [];
}

edge Contains { }
edge Produces { }
edge Emits { has lane: int = 0; }
edge Crosses { }
edge Reenters { }

walker RtiCompiler {
    has image: RtiImage;
    has seen_federates: list[str] = [];
    has seen_flows: list[str] = [];
    has seen_boundaries: list[str] = [];

    can begin with Root entry {
        print("compile canonical federation without graph re-analysis");
        visit [->:Contains:->] else { disengage; }
    }

    can lower_federate with Federate entry {
        if here.federate_id in self.seen_federates {
            print(f"cycle guard: federate {here.federate_id}");
            skip;
        }
        self.seen_federates.append(here.federate_id);
        self.image.federate_table.append(
            f"{here.federate_id}@logical={here.logical_time}@lifecycle={here.lifecycle_policy}"
        );
        print(f"federate {here.federate_id} keeps logical time {here.logical_time}");
        visit [->:Emits:->] else { disengage; }
    }

    can lower_flow with Flow entry {
        if here.flow_id in self.seen_flows {
            print(f"cycle guard: flow {here.flow_id}");
            skip;
        }
        self.seen_flows.append(here.flow_id);

        policy_ok = here.recovery_policy == "retry" and
            here.boundary_policy == "fail-closed" and
            here.transport_policy == "in-memory" and
            here.codec_policy == "binary" and
            here.timing_policy == "logical" and
            here.security_policy == "authenticated";
        if not policy_ok {
            here.available = False;
            print(f"rejected unsupported policy for {here.flow_id}");
            skip;
        }
        if self.image.frozen {
            print(f"rejected mutation after freeze for {here.flow_id}");
            disengage;
        }
        self.image.flow_table.append(f"{here.flow_id}:delay={here.delay_ms}");
        self.image.policy_table.append(
            f"{here.flow_id}:{here.recovery_policy}:{here.boundary_policy}:{here.transport_policy}"
        );
        print(f"flow {here.flow_id} preserves delay {here.delay_ms}ms");
        visit [->:Crosses:->] else { disengage; }
    }

    can lower_boundary with Boundary entry {
        if here.boundary_id in self.seen_boundaries {
            print(f"cycle guard: boundary {here.boundary_id}");
            skip;
        }
        self.seen_boundaries.append(here.boundary_id);
        self.image.boundary_table.append(
            f"{here.boundary_id}:{here.physical_role}:{here.direction}"
        );
        print(f"boundary {here.boundary_id} survives physical lowering");
        visit [-->] else { disengage; }
    }

    can summarize with Root exit {
        print(f"dense image {self.image.image_id}: {len(self.image.federate_table)} federates, "
            f"{len(self.image.flow_table)} flows, {len(self.image.boundary_table)} boundaries");
    }
}

with entry {
    image = RtiImage(
        title="compiled federation image",
        image_id="rti-image-5a"
    );
    root +>:Produces:+> image;

    west = Federate(
        title="West",
        federate_id="fed-west",
        logical_time=12,
        lifecycle_policy="coordinated"
    );
    east = Federate(
        title="East",
        federate_id="fed-east",
        logical_time=12,
        lifecycle_policy="coordinated"
    );
    route_a = Flow(
        title="West to East",
        flow_id="flow-west-east",
        delay_ms=20,
        recovery_policy="retry",
        boundary_policy="fail-closed",
        transport_policy="in-memory",
        codec_policy="binary",
        timing_policy="logical",
        security_policy="authenticated"
    );
    route_b = Flow(
        title="East to West",
        flow_id="flow-east-west",
        delay_ms=35,
        recovery_policy="retry",
        boundary_policy="fail-closed",
        transport_policy="in-memory",
        codec_policy="binary",
        timing_policy="logical",
        security_policy="authenticated"
    );
    west_boundary = Boundary(
        title="West output",
        boundary_id="boundary-west-output",
        physical_role="output",
        direction="west-to-east"
    );
    east_boundary = Boundary(
        title="East output",
        boundary_id="boundary-east-output",
        physical_role="output",
        direction="east-to-west"
    );

    root +>:Contains:+> west;
    root +>:Contains:+> east;
    west +>:Emits(lane=1):+> route_a;
    east +>:Emits(lane=2):+> route_b;
    route_a +>:Crosses:+> west_boundary;
    route_b +>:Crosses:+> east_boundary;
    west_boundary +>:Reenters:+> route_a;
    east_boundary +>:Reenters:+> route_b;

    compiler = RtiCompiler(image=image);
    root spawn compiler;
    image.frozen = True;
    print(f"image {image.image_id} frozen={image.frozen}");
}

