"""Subtree authority: a parent key can act on any account in its subtree.

Models the aios issue natively — accounts are nodes connected by typed
``HasChild`` edges, an actor's subtree is discovered by a walker that
descends through children, and an ``Authority`` walker enforces the
invariant: an actor may act on a target iff the target is the actor
itself or lies in the actor's subtree. An archived account in the chain
breaks subtree authority at that node.
