"""Frame-time scratch-buffer thrash: reserve() and shrink() fight each other.

Models the issue's hot path natively:
- Per-frame scratch buffers for draw batches (reserve on wrong quantity,
  shrink on the right quantity) and for sibling scratches (working set
  matches reserve) for comparison.
- A walker audits each scratch buffer every "frame" and reports whether
  the reserve/shrink pair thrashes (realloc each frame) or amortizes.
